    "created_at": "2021-02-26T23:58:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-02-26T23:59:51Z",
    "body": "The culprit seems to be in [this block](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/modules/git_commit.rs#L50) of code. It seems that this will only find annotated tags in the repository, while lightweight tags don't appear in the list of tags.\r\n\r\n@mantzas @dycw Could you confirm that the tags which aren't currently appearing are lightweight tags? The only way I've found of doing this is using `git show <tagname>`. An annotated tag will show both an annotation commit and the base commit, while a lightweight tag will only show a base commit. In the following image, I have tags named `annotated` and `lightweight`, which are annotated and lightweight tags, respectively.\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4605384/109367593-1a63bb00-785c-11eb-9449-aca371c8b962.png)\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
