    "created_at": "2021-08-15T13:05:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-08-15T13:06:28Z",
    "body": "I think this is also partly a missing feature, so maybe this discussion is worth forking into a separate issue.\r\n\r\nIn addition to displaying both annotated and lightweight git tags, I would expect any git tags to be shown always by default, whether in a detached state or not. That is, the commit hash is more useful when detached, but it would be nicer to always show the tag on the head of the current branch.\r\n\r\nThis could mean either changing the default behavior, (in which case disabling tags means removing them from the format string), or changing the config, which could mean adding a `tag_always` key, or changing `tag_disabled` to also accept a string. The config changes seem a bit awkward while keeping backwards compatibility.\r\n\r\nThe most elegant solution imho would be splitting the `git_commit` module into a `git_commit` proper and a `git_tag`, which would also ensure no extra `()` are displayed when the commit hash is not shown.\r\n\r\nI could do this rework if you're willing to merge something along these lines.",
